      "modify_from": "When target_visits is zero and the instructed cube is not held, approach vertically above its center at z=0.15 m, gripper open, with roll approximately pi, pitch zero and yaw aligned to its square edges. If already above it at that height, visually recenter before descending: back-project the cube's top-face center onto approximately z=0.04 m, then command that horizontal center at TCP z=0.02 m and close. The projection plane and grasp TCP height are different. Do not copy the reported hover TCP x,y merely because it is approximately aligned; correct ordinary hover tracking error in the descent.",
      "modify_to": "When target_visits is zero and the instructed cube is not held, use the center of its top square face for both the initial hover and grasp descent, excluding visible side faces from the center estimate. Intersect that pixel's calibrated camera ray with the plane approximately z=0.04 m to obtain world x,y. Approach at that x,y and TCP z=0.15 m with the gripper open, roll approximately pi, pitch zero, and yaw aligned to the top-face edges transformed into world coordinates. Do not infer yaw from a nominal 45-degree rotation or an uncorrected image-edge angle. If already above the cube at hover height, recompute the top-face center from the current calibrated wrist image and command the resulting world x,y at TCP z=0.02 m and close. Neither the hover height nor the grasp TCP height is the projection plane. Do not copy the reported hover TCP x,y merely because it is approximately aligned; correct ordinary hover tracking error in the descent."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "No memory fields or filling rules are changed. Current calibrated images supply the pickup geometry; no pickup-stage field, localization memory, or episode-specific coordinates are added. The right_target_center field is retained: this round provides no evidence overturning the earlier demonstrated need during occlusion. All earlier target and button localization edits remain in force."
}
